{"name":"Powder Puff","hex":"#ffeff3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"powder puff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball or pad of soft material used for the application of cosmetic powder to the face.","Any of certain species of genus Calliandra."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of powderpuff."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder_puff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Powder puff","blocks":[{"text":"Powder puffs are pieces of soft material used for the application of face powder. They may be shaped as balls or pads."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Makeup_Powder_Puffs_-_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CE%BC_%CF%80%CE%BF%CE%BD_%CE%BC%CE%B1%CE%BA%CE%B9%CE%B3%CE%B9%CE%B1%CE%B6.JPG/330px-Makeup_Powder_Puffs_-_%CE%A0%CE%BF%CE%BC_%CF%80%CE%BF%CE%BD_%CE%BC%CE%B1%CE%BA%CE%B9%CE%B3%CE%B9%CE%B1%CE%B6.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder_puff"},{"title":"Powder","blocks":[{"text":"A powder is a dry solid composed of many very fine particles that may flow freely when shaken or tilted. Powders are a special sub-class of granular materials, although the terms powder and granular are sometimes used to distinguish separate classes of material. In particular, powders refer to those granular materials that have the finer grain sizes, and that therefore have a greater tendency to form clumps when flowing. Granulars refer to the coarser granular materials that do not tend to form clumps except when wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Iron_powder.JPG/330px-Iron_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Bailey-powder-puff-1892.jpg/500px-Bailey-powder-puff-1892.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content